## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical RHCSA skills applying to real-world multi-tenant TLS proxying, container runtimes, SNIs, firewall rules, SELinux, systemd upgrade churn, and test planning.

## Key Concepts
- Podman containers and nginx as TLS-terminating reverse proxy
- SNI-based routing, Per-tenant backends
- nftables rate limiting per tenant
- Vault integration and live cert reload
- Zero-downtime upgrades and SELinux policy

## Code Example
```
# example nginx snippet per tenant
server {
  listen 8443 ssl;
  server_name tenantA.example.com;
  ssl_certificate /vault/certs/tenantA.crt;
  ssl_certificate_key /vault/certs/tenantA.key;
  location / { proxy_pass https://10.0.3.21:8443; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant rate limits under surge?
- How would you roll back a failed cert rotation?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluate ability to implement host integrity controls with minimal downtime using native RH tooling, idempotence, and rollback.

## Key Concepts

- rpm -V usage for binary integrity
- systemd service and timer
- Baseline diffing and logging
- Alerting and rollback strategy
- Reinstall path from diffs

## Code Example

```javascript
const { execSync } = require('child_process');
const fs = require('fs');
const baseline = '/var/log/integrity/baseline.txt';
const current = execSync('rpm -V -a').toString();
const base = fs.readFileSync(baseline, 'utf8');
const nl = String.fromCharCode(10);
const diff = current.split(/\\r?\\n/).filter(l => !base.includes(l)).join(nl);
if (diff) {
  fs.appendFileSync('/var/log/sys_integrity.log', diff + nl);
  console.log('ALERT');
} else {
  console.log('OK');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this for multi-host environments and centralize reporting?
- How would you minimize false positives around legitimate upgrades?
